3. Architecture: Embodied Social Foundation Model (ESFM)

3.1 Hierarchical Temporal Decomposition

The ESFM architecture consists of three layers operating at distinct temporal frequencies to balance computational tractability with real-time responsiveness.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│  RELATIONAL LAYER (>200 ms)         │
│  • Beta trust update (per dimension)│
│  • Cultural prior adaptation        │
│  • Explanation style selection      │
│  • Hierarchical MAP personalization │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
                ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│  SOCIAL LAYER (10–200 ms)           │
│  • Particle-filtered intent inference│
│  • Bounded-depth S-ToM update       │
│  • Golden-ratio proxemic cost map   │
│  • Bi-level optimization solver     │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
                ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│  REACTIVE LAYER (<10 ms)            │
│  • ORCA/CBF collision avoidance     │
│  • Emergency stop triggers          │
│  • Sensor fusion (RGB-D, LiDAR)    │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Cross-Layer Communication: Structured messages ensure type safety and decoupling:

