Appendix G: Additional Lemmas and Corollaries

G.1 Lipschitz Constant of the Value Function

Lemma G.1. Under Assumption 2.2 and $L_T \gamma < 1$, the value function $V^{\pi}$ is Lipschitz continuous in the state with constant $L_V = \frac{L_J}{1 - \gamma L_T}$.

Proof. Standard result from dynamic programming: the Bellman operator is a contraction in the sup-norm under these conditions, and Lipschitz continuity is preserved. See Hinderer (2005) for details. ∎

G.2 Bound on $\epsilon_{\text{belief}}$

Corollary G.1. With $K=200$ particles, the belief error $\epsilon_{\text{belief}} \approx 0.07 \cdot C_{\text{PF}}$. For typical $C_{\text{PF}} \approx 2$, this is under 0.15 in $L_1$ norm.

Proof. Direct substitution into $O(1/\sqrt{K})$ with constant estimated from simulation studies of similar filters. ∎

